// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Attempts of Kerberos Coercion Via DNS SPN Spoofing
// Sigma ID: 0ed99dda-6a35-11ef-8c99-0242ac120002
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-06-20 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: collection, credential-access, persistence, privilege-escalation, T1557.001, T1187
// Description: Detects the presence of "UWhRC....AAYBAAAA" pattern in command line. The pattern
//   "1UWhRCAAAAA..BAAAA" is a base64-encoded signature that corresponds to a marshaled
//   CREDENTIAL_TARGET_INFORMATION structure. Attackers can use this technique to coerce
//   authentication from victim systems to attacker-controlled hosts. It is one of the strong
//   indicators of a Kerberos coercion attack, where adversaries manipulate DNS records to spoof
//   Service Principal Names (SPNs) and redirect authentication requests like in CVE-2025-33073. If
//   you see this pattern in the command line, it is likely an attempt to add spoofed Service
//   Principal Names (SPNs) to DNS records, or checking for the presence of such records through the
//   `nslookup` command.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.synacktiv.com/en/publications/ntlm-reflection-is-dead-long-live-ntlm-reflection-an-in-depth-analysis-of-cve-2025
//   - https://googleprojectzero.blogspot.com/2021/10/using-kerberos-for-authentication-relay.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_kerberos_coercion_via_dns_spn_spoofing.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "UWhRCA" and ProcessCommandLine contains "BAAAA"
